  "behavior": {
    "threshold": "Power mode and a separate enabled flag govern the entire -100..0 dBFS range; finite above-threshold values activate, equality does not. Off and CTCSS clearly disable this power-based feature.",
    "native": "Only complete production RF FFT windows advance observation time. Current control version, generation and epoch are required; partial windows, stalled input, resets and future timestamps cannot renew a measurement. Expiry is max(500 ms, 2.5 capture-block durations).",
    "daemon": "Acknowledged capture geometry, gain and finite applied threshold precede a fresh tagged raw spectrum observation. Gain and VFO changes retire previous measurements. Receipt age and unique frame timestamps govern expiry; frozen displays and hidden Listen tabs continue measurement ingestion. Scanner and monitor share the scanner observation token without superseding each other, and scanner startup cannot inherit the monitor token.",
    "counts": "Successful local open increments once. Daemon command queue acceptance records a pending start; only a current-session active acknowledgement for the owned channel increments. Failure, timeout, duplicate status, cancelled starts and closed queues do not count. Pending starts/stops prevent repeated commands, and failed starts have a one-second retry delay.",
    "queue": "Recording progress coalesces within a phase, preserving start/stop acknowledgements in FIFO order and retaining the existing 64-event bound."
  },
